  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe cause is the dive start. The verify reading is correct.\n\n- A bore-side contour cuts only its ring. It does not cut the core inside the ring.\n- On a later level the Ramp chord is blocked, so `substituted_dive` takes over. `dive_point` puts the dive a wall margin inward from the cut path, at radius 6.55. The tool footprint then reaches the uncut core, which stands at the carried stock top (Z 5).\n- The old code started the rapid at the plane above plus the plunge height (Z 2). Verify found `RapidInStock` on the second level. This conviction is correct.\n\nThe fix is in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_bore.rs`:\n\n- The new function `column_top` gives the material top at the dive point. It is the plane above when the point is on the cut path, or when an earlier plunge opened that column. Else it is the top of the material.\n- The substituted dive and the Plunge arm use this value for the rapid height.\n- Later levels keep the short rapid over the plane above, because the first dive opened the column.\n- No check is weakened. No new operation parameter: there is no strategy choice.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/2301-bore-ramp-carried-stock.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Old code: planar and retract links give `RapidInStock { at: 2673 }`. The plunge start Zs are `[2.0, 0.0, -2.0]`.\n- New code: verify is empty. The plunge start Zs are `[7.0, 0.0, -2.0]`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/motion/tests/bore_carried_ramp.rs`:\n\n- `the_bore_dive_under_carried_stock_starts_over_the_core`: red on the old code (`RapidInStock`), green with the fix.\n- `the_later_bore_dives_start_over_the_plane_above`: red on the old code (left `[2.0, 0.0, -2.0]`, right `[7.0, 0.0, -2.0]`), green with the fix.\n\n## Gate\n\nThe quick plan (`--base origin/main`) has 8 steps. I ran each suite directly with cargo:\n\n- motion lib: 411 passed.\n- motion tests `bore_carried_ramp`, `contour_inside_ramp`, `entry_approach`, `entry_ramp_angle`, `one_descent`: all pass.\n- app `carried_stock_entry`: 5 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Overlap with PR #2013\n\nPR #2013 changes the `mat_top` and `from` lines of `bore_entry`. This PR changes the `sub` closure, the Plunge arm and new helpers in the same function. `git merge-tree` of this head with `origin/issue/2004-top-z-level` is clean. When PR #2013 takes this fix, it can remove the `known` skip of the case `carried bore lead linear Ramp planar/retract`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The combined behaviour with PR #2013 was not built or run. Only the textual merge was checked.\n- The off-path start of the Helix arm.\n- The app golden suites other than `carried_stock_entry`. Without carried stock the output is the same, because on the second level the plane above equals the entry top.\n\nChangelog: Bore contour: a Ramp entry under carried stock no longer rapids into the uncut core on the second level.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nFixes #2301\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
